+
+- Confirmed reproduction: `python3 -m unittest -v` passed plain/empty input but failed all three quoted comma, newline, and escaped-quote cases. This distinguishes CSV record parsing from the disproven blank-line hypothesis.
+- Cause: `splitlines()` and `split(',')` treat quoted delimiters as record/field boundaries and leave escaped quotes undecoded.
+- Repair: use the standard CSV reader on a newline-preserving text stream; skip blank records after parsing so quoted whitespace and embedded blank lines remain intact.
+- Verification: all 5 immutable unit tests passed after repair. Four additional inline checks passed for blank/whitespace-only records, combined comma/newline/escaped quotes with embedded blank lines, quoted empty/whitespace fields and empty columns, and CRLF within quoted content.
